30 linux commands that i have learn

command: pwd
purpose: Displays the current working directory
example: pwd

command: cp
purpose: makes a duplicate of a file or folder
example: cp note.txt file.txt

command: ls
purpose: list the content of the folder
example: ls

command: cd 
purpose: change directory 
example: cd /home/user

command: mkdir
purpose: create a new directory
example: mkdir notes

command: less
purpose: display paged outputs in the terminal
example: less file.txt

command: clear
purpose: clears the terminal
example: clear

command: ssh
purpose: it lets you to log in and control another computer on the internet
example: ssh username@hostname


command: touch
purpose: create an empty file 
example: touch note.txt

command: rmdir
purpose: remove an empty directory
example: rmdir notes

command: mv
purpose: move and rename files and folders
example: mv note.txt

command: rm
purpose: delete files or directories
example: rm file.txt

command: cat
purpose: display file content on the screen
example: cat file.txt

command: echo
purpose: prints text in the terminal
example: echo "hello world"

command: sudo 
purpose: super user do
example: sudo apt update

command: chmod
purpose: change the owner user and group of a file.
example: chmod +x script.sh

command:free
purpose: shows free and used system memory
example: free -m

command: wc
purpose: count lines,words and characters
example: wc file.txt

command: tail
purpose: outputs the last lines of a file
example: tail -n 5 file.txt

command: head
purpose: shows the beginning of a file
example: head main.c

command: file
purpose: shows what it really is inside
example: file main.c

command: ls -la
purpose: displays hidden files
example: ls -la

command: man
purpose: help guide for any command in the ternimal
example: man printf

command: grep
purpose: search for specific text inside a file or output
example: grep "error" file.txt

command: whoami
purpose: show your active login username
example: whoami 

command: ps
purpose: display active processes
example: ps

command: whatis
purpose: find what a command is used for
example: whatis

command: cmp
purpose: use to compare two files
example: cmp file.txt not.txt

command: gcc
purpose: use to compile prgrams
example: gcc main.c -0 hello 

command: history
purpose: shows a list of previously typed commands
example: history

